\p{Filed under [[conf-neuromod-nyc-2026]], category 2 (imaging-derived targeting). Projected talk slide; audience cropped out.}

\image{conf-fox-targeting-talk.jpg}

\p{\strong{Caption.} A targeting talk making the case that \em{where} you stimulate is the whole game: \strong{connectivity-based} targeting (via fMRI cortico-subcortical connection and drug-cue reactivity maps) versus \strong{scalp-based} targeting, with a depression trial (MADRS) showing the connectivity-guided target outperforming. Cites Taylor et al. 2026 (JAMA Psychiatry). Same thesis as [[conf-siddiqi-impulsivity-mapping]] — the target is an imaging inference, not a scalp landmark.}
